    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (66.62) and **Zack Gelof** (66.21) anchor our lineup, serving as the clear priority starts. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** benefits from a strong middle-of-the-order positioning, and despite facing a steady arm in J. Soriano, his elite offensive profile holds high leverage even in neutral conditions. Meanwhile, **Zack Gelof** draws the highest ceiling projection of the day due to a favorable matchup against Kade Anderson (5.25 xERA). The significant 19% boost from the opposing SP skill, combined with a premium #2 spot in the order, positions **Zack Gelof** as our primary source of run production today. **Jonathan Aranda** (63.13) also stands out as a strong play, as the platoon advantage against Quantrill pushes his score well above his baseline, making him a high-efficiency anchor at first base.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the card involved the fringe outfield and utility spots, specifically the choice to start **Dylan Beavers** (52.94) over potential alternatives. While **Dylan Beavers** faces a left-on-left disadvantage against Bennett, his score was buoyed by a substantial 16% park factor benefit and an opportunistic stolen base environment against a pitcher with slow delivery\u2014a critical metric for our roster strategy given our focus on the scarcity of SB. Conversely, **Braden Montgomery** (47.15) and **Alex Freeland** (46.84) hover near the marginal floor. **Alex Freeland** remains a risk due to the #9 lineup slot, which severely suppresses his scoring potential despite his versatility as a switch hitter. \n\nWe must remain cautious with our \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Will Smith**, **Lawrence Butler**, and **Cal Raleigh**. While these players are currently projected for strong scores, any shift downward in their batting order could rapidly deflate their efficiency rankings. We are currently navigating a depleted bench; with **Bryce Harper** and **Justin Crawford** inactive, and both **Tyler Freeman** and **Matt Chapman** sidelined by minors/IL designations, we have little room to pivot if these late-afternoon lineups are unfavorable. Keep a close watch on **Lawrence Butler**; while his SP matchup is elite, his raw score is already being held back by a 13% platoon penalty, making him the most sensitive to any negative lineup adjustments.",
